1. She previously worked in a developer job that she deeply disliked, which contributed to her decision to pursue VTubing. (Verbatim: "i really hated my previous job i really hated it... i wouldn't have been so motivated to do something else... to work towards vtubing")

2. Her negative experiences at her previous job, including gender-based pay discrimination and forced socialization, pushed her to reconsider her career and life goals. (Verbatim: "paying me less because i'm a woman kind of thing or you know all of that awful things... that negative stuff pushed me to really think harder about like what i actually want to do")

3. She wanted to become a developer because she believed it would allow her to work from home and avoid extensive communication with others. (Verbatim: "i always thought that like i wanted to be a developer the idea was if i was a developer i could work on the computer i could chill at home and i would have fun coding... i wouldn't have to communicate with people")

4. She views companies that emphasize forced "family" culture as a red flag. (Verbatim: "it's a definitely a red flag right of a company where it's like we're just family... i need a salary yo i have a family")

5. During job interviews, she felt pressured to give insincere, overly enthusiastic answers rather than honest ones. (Verbatim: "i had to be like oh i'm just... really passionate about about financial programs yo... or i can give you the fake cancer where i talk about how i've always wanted to be a cashier")

6. She attended school where she had a difficult friendship with someone who strongly identified with the quote "if you can't handle me at my worst, you don't deserve me at my best." (Verbatim: "in school i had like this one friend in quotes... she heckin loved that if you can't handle me at my worst you don't deserve me at my best quote")

7. She believes people should not have to earn someone’s best effort or kindness, and that one should strive to always offer their best. (Verbatim: "i'll always give my best you don't have to earn my best... i should be providing my best whether or not you've handled me at my worst")

8. She was raised with the belief that one must be perfect or the effort is pointless, a mindset she now recognizes as unhealthy. (Verbatim: "my parents always taught me perfect or pointless perfection or nothing mate")

9. She struggles with perfectionism and feels called out by the idea of "striving for progress, not perfection." (Verbatim: "this one feels like it's calling me out for always trying to get perfection")

10. She finds motivation in the concept of visible progress, such as an XP bar in video games, and believes it could help in real life. (Verbatim: "progress is imagining you have an xp bar and even when you fail you do gain xp") [end of text]



